<title>FINLAND: Finnish state airports move 6.2 pct more cargo '96.</title>
<headline>Finnish state airports move 6.2 pct more cargo '96.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish state-owned airports' inbound and outbound cargo volumes rose 6.2 percent to 90,093 tonnes in 1996 compared with 1995, Finland's Civil Aviation Authority said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The authority, which manages 25 airports in Finland, released the following figures about its cargo volumes. No further information was available.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for the authority said small corrections could be expected from some airports, but these would affect the totals only marginally.</p>
<p>FREIGHT (Inbound, outbound in tonnes)</p>
<p>		1996	 1995</p>
<p> January    6,662	6,349</p>
<p> February   7,126	7,075</p>
<p> March	7,716	7,496</p>
<p> April	6,384	6,540</p>
<p> May	  6,758	6,780</p>
<p> June	 7,187	7,158</p>
<p> July	 7,052	6,493</p>
<p> August     7,989	6,876</p>
<p> September  7,951	7,217</p>
<p> October    8,435	7,700</p>
<p> November   8,431	7,608</p>
<p> December   8,402	7,520</p>
<p> TOTAL     90,093     84,812</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
